\ Bounded-memory regression for iterator allocations.
\
\ Every #map, #filter, #take, #drop, and >iterator used to allocate its
\ Iterator struct on the context arena, and >iterator on a non-array
\ sequence also parked its materialized slice there, so this loop grew by
\ a few hundred bytes per iteration and exhausted the 4 MB cap set in the
\ `.flags` sidecar partway through. Iterators are refcounted on the
\ general allocator now: draining #collect drops the last reference,
\ which frees the struct and its materialized backing, so the loop stays
\ flat and prints the marker.

10000 [
  { 1 2 3 4 } [ 2 * ] #map #collect drop
  "ab" >iterator #collect drop
] times

"flat" print-line
